    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0158" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00/18½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">12 March, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I wish you would be kind
                    enough to formulate a careful and conclusive memorandum for the use of the
                    committee of the Senate with regard to the enclosed resolution.<anchor n="81"
                        xml:id="d80-f1"/> I take it for granted that you feel as I do that this is
                    no time to act as the resolution prescribes, and certainly when I pronounced for
                    open diplomacy, I meant not that there should be no private discussions <pb
                        facs="0159" n="113" xml:id="pg113"/> of delicate matters, but that no secret
                    agreements of any sort should be entered into and that all international
                    relations, when fixed, should be open, above-board, and explicit.</p>
                <p>Cordially and sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d80-f1" n="81" xml:id="d80-f1-content">
                <p>For text of resolution, see enclosure to the following document.</p>
